* The west sea's seabed airlock (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own
* script; art from tools/sprites/westlock.py). Run by openc2e after the world
* loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
*
* The west sea (rooms 121-137) has one way to land: up at the surface. A
* creature that sank to the seabed found no way out on foot and drowned
* there (owner, 2026-11-12: "should we create some sort of airlock thing
* around here?"; chose the seabed airlock). The seabed slopes down to its
* low point by the rock wall (x ~650, floor y ~1365), where stranded
* creatures end up.
*
* A round sea door is set in the rock at the foot of the slope (x 600-656,
* left of the game's own rock, which is drawn over everything from x ~650;
* 2 3 247, sprite zwsd), and a
* brass land door (2 3 248, zwld) in the west wall of the shallow pool just
* east of it (room 110, x 669-1170, water 1352-1440; owner, 2026-11-16, its
* place chosen from airlock-pool-exit-mockup2.png). An invisible car
* (vehicle 3 2 151, zwcr) waits at the sea door. When a creature is at the
* low point the sea door opens and the car takes it in, pulls it down fast
* (as if sucked in), shuts the door behind it, drains the chamber for a
* moment, and shoots it out of the land door into the pool, facing east;
* the door shuts again. From the pool it wades east and walks out up the far
* bank (room 113, then 108 and the rest of the world). While it rides, the
* rock (2 3 249, zwrk, cut from the player's own background) is drawn in
* front of it, with the doorways left open.
*
* Until 2026-11-16 the land door was in the rock face at the east end of the
* floor by the cage lift (room 120, floor 1540). That floor opens only into
* a corridor (rooms 120, 119, 118 and the seam alcove 180) with no way out
* on foot, only two cage lifts: rescued creatures spent a median 355
* decisions there and many starved. The rooms changed for that exit (1.
* below) are kept; they do no harm.
*
* 1. The floor by the lift (room 120) was 68 px tall and its doorway to the
*    lift's room (119) was too small for creatures (100; creatures are 224).
*    Its ceiling rises to 1400 (the seabed room above, 121, ends there now;
*    its floor line is kept) and the doorway opens. ROOM takes all of a
*    room's data, so each room's own values are passed back.
doif room 121 3 eq 1472
  room 121 399 1220 669 1400 room 121 4 room 121 5 room 121 6 room 121 7 room 121 8 room 121 9 room 121 12 room 121 13 room 121 14 room 121 15 room 121 16 room 121 17 room 121 19
  ssfc 121 4 0 163 60 93 150 83 270 28
  room 120 399 1400 573 1540 room 120 4 room 120 5 room 120 6 room 120 7 room 120 8 room 120 9 room 120 12 room 120 13 room 120 14 room 120 15 room 120 16 room 120 17 room 120 19
endi
setv door 0 120 119 255
*
* 1b. Objects that crossed from the floor room into room 115 (east, from y
*    1472) with their tops above 1472 were stopped by physics there, partly
*    in the rock, and hung (two 2 5 2 and a 2 15 9, 2026-11-15). The engine
*    now sets such an object back in and lets it fall
*    (Agent::healOutOfRoomSystem), once it moves; these are given a push.
enum 2 0 0
  setv var1 attr andv var1 128
  setv var2 posl addv var2 posr divv var2 2
  doif var1 ne 0 doif var2 ge 560 doif var2 le 680 doif posb ge 1440 doif posb le 1545 doif vely eq 0
    setv vely 1
  endi endi endi endi endi endi
next
*
* 1c. Room 108's floor (x 1342-1473, floor 1300) has a doorway (50) to room
*    112 below, but the rooms do not touch: 140 px of rock lie between
*    (112's top is 1440). A creature or object falling onto that floor went
*    through it into the rock, out of the room map, and on down to rooms 112
*    and 114, the lower west cave, whose only way up is the cage lift into
*    the corridor of 1. (two of three test creatures dropped there, 2026-11-16).
*    Creatures let out into the pool (3.) walk out over this floor, so it is
*    closed.
setv door 0 108 112 0
*
* 2. The doors (the sea door behind creatures, plane 1400; the land door
*    9000, see below) and the rock in front of a rider (plane 1550; riders
*    are at 1501).
enum 2 3 247 kill targ next
inst new: simp zwsd 6 0 1400 0 setv cls2 2 3 247 setv attr 0 mvto 600 1302 slow
enum 2 3 248 kill targ next
* (the land door in front of the game's own rock over the pool's west bank,
* scenery cvl2/cvlk at plane 8999, as in the approved mock-up; behind it,
* at 1400, it was hidden; creatures at the pool's very west edge pass
* behind it)
inst new: simp zwld 5 0 9000 0 setv cls2 2 3 248 setv attr 0 mvto 662 1366 slow
enum 2 3 249 kill targ next
inst new: simp zwrk 1 0 1550 0 setv cls2 2 3 249 setv attr 0 mvto 573 1245 slow
*
* 3. The car: its box (48 x 110, bottom at the low point's floor) is where
*    it picks up. OV00 its state (0 waiting, 1 sea door opening, 2 stepping
*    in, 3 going down, 4 draining, 5 to the land door, 6 letting out), OV01 a
*    count of ticks, OV02 set once the sea door has shut behind it.
enum 3 2 151 kill targ next
inst
new: vhcl zwcr 1 0
setv cls2 3 2 151
new: part 0 0 0 0 1501
cabn 0 0 48 110
cabp 1501
setv attr 16
bhvr 0 0
setv ov00 0 setv ov01 0 setv ov02 0
mvto 604 1245
tick 1
slow

* every tick, all at once (INST)
scrp 3 2 151 9
  inst
  addv ov01 1
  * waiting: every 10 ticks, look for a creature at the low point
  doif ov00 eq 0
    doif ov01 lt 10 stop endi
    setv ov01 0
    setv var0 0
    * (not one it has just let out into the pool, OV94 1: the pool's west
    * end meets the seabed's low point at about the same height, x 669, so
    * creatures wading back to the pool's west wall were taken in again and
    * again; the mark is cleared once it has left the pool's area)
    enum 4 0 0
      setv var1 posl addv var1 posr divv var1 2
      doif ov94 eq 1
        setv var2 1
        doif var1 lt 560 setv var2 0 endi
        doif var1 gt 1200 setv var2 0 endi
        doif posb lt 1250 setv var2 0 endi
        doif posb gt 1470 setv var2 0 endi
        doif var2 eq 0 setv ov94 0 endi
      endi
      doif ov94 eq 0 doif var1 ge 585 doif var1 le 669 doif posb ge 1330 doif posb le 1400
        setv var0 1
      endi endi endi endi endi
    next
    doif var0 eq 1
      enum 2 3 247 pose 1 next
      setv ov00 1
    endi
    stop
  endi
  * the sea door opens; the creature is taken in
  doif ov00 eq 1
    doif ov01 eq 2 enum 2 3 247 snde dor1 anim [2345] next endi
    doif ov01 lt 14 stop endi
    gpas
    setv ov00 2 setv ov01 0
    stop
  endi
  * stepping in: into the middle of the doorway (the car is there already)
  doif ov00 eq 2
    setv ov00 3 setv ov01 0
    stop
  endi
  * going down, fast, as if sucked in (owner, 2026-11-13: it moved at lift
  * speed; 16 px a tick, was 4); the sea door shuts once the rider is below
  doif ov00 eq 3
    * not perfectly smooth (owner, 2026-11-15: "the slightest of
    * jerkiness"): 12-20 px a tick, and about one tick in eight it holds
    rndv var1 0 7
    doif var1 eq 0 stop endi
    rndv var1 12 20
    setv var0 post addv var0 var1
    * (down to the pool's level: the car's bottom 1418, 4 px over the
    * pool's bed where the rider is let out; 1428, room 120's floor, before)
    doif var0 ge 1290
      doif ov02 eq 0 setv ov02 1 enum 2 3 247 snde dor1 anim [54321] next endi
    endi
    doif var0 ge 1308 setv var0 1308 setv ov00 4 setv ov01 0 snde bubb endi
    mvto posl var0
    stop
  endi
  * draining (briefly), then the land door opens
  doif ov00 eq 4
    doif ov01 eq 4 enum 2 3 248 snde dor1 anim [1234] next endi
    doif ov01 lt 12 stop endi
    setv ov00 5 setv ov01 0
    stop
  endi
  * to the land door: in one move, from the rock into the pool just east
  * of the door (the car x 716-764, bottom 1418: the pool's bed slopes from
  * 1372 at its west wall to 1432, and is about 1422 under the car's middle;
  * set down wholly inside the pool room and a little above its bed, or the
  * physics finds a corner outside the rooms and pushes it up)
  doif ov00 eq 5
    mvto 716 post
    setv ov00 6 setv ov01 0
    stop
  endi
  * letting out: shot out of the land door, east into the pool (owner,
  * 2026-11-13: "it should shoot them out the exit"; gentler than the old
  * shot across a dry floor, as it lands in water); the land door shutting,
  * back to wait at the sea door
  doif ov00 eq 6
    doif ov01 eq 2
      dpas
      enum 4 0 0
        setv var1 posl addv var1 posr divv var1 2
        doif var1 ge 690 doif var1 le 800 doif posb ge 1330 doif posb le 1445
          setv velx 14 setv vely -5 setv ov94 1
        endi endi endi endi
      next
    endi
    doif ov01 eq 30 enum 2 3 248 snde dor1 anim [3210] next endi
    doif ov01 lt 40 stop endi
    mvto 604 1245
    enum 2 3 247 pose 0 next
    setv ov00 0 setv ov01 0 setv ov02 0
  endi
endm

* 4. The sea current down to the hatch (owner, 2026-11-16: drowning was the
*    second biggest avoidable death in Home, and the west sea's shelf the
*    spot it kept happening: rooms 134 and 135, x 500-840, floors at y
*    1096-1140 in open water above the rock, three times in the notes
*    before this and once more in a test copy that day). A creature that
*    sinks onto that shelf stands on the boundary between water rooms, high
*    above the seabed (rooms 204 and 121 below it), and never reaches the
*    hatch's pickup point at the seabed's low point (x 585-669, feet
*    1330-1400); it drowns where it stands. A watcher (2 1 160, every 2 s)
*    counts how long each live creature has stood on the shelf (OV92) and,
*    after about 20 s (so a creature passing is not swept off), starts a
*    current (2 1 161) that carries it, not quite smoothly (as the other
*    rides), west along the shelf into open water (x 530), down through
*    room 204 to the seabed (feet 1365), and east to the low point, where
*    the hatch takes it in as it would anyone. Moved by script (MVTO with
*    WAIT 1), so it is no fall to learn from or be hurt by. OV93 marks one
*    being carried.
enum 2 1 160 kill targ next
enum 2 1 161 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 160 setv attr 16 mvto 5000 1350 tick 20 slow
scrp 2 1 160 9
  inst
  enum 4 0 0
    doif dead eq 0 and ov93 eq 0
      setv var0 posl
      addv var0 posr
      divv var0 2
      setv var1 0
      doif var0 ge 500 and var0 le 840 and posb ge 1080 and posb le 1145
        setv var1 1
      endi
      doif var1 eq 1
        addv ov92 1
        doif ov92 ge 10
          setv ov92 0
          setv ov93 1
          setv var8 targ
          new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 161 setv attr 16 setv ov00 var8 mvto 5000 1360 tick 1
          targ var8
        endi
      else
        setv ov92 0
      endi
    endi
  next
endm
* The current: carries its creature (OV00), then is removed.
scrp 2 1 161 9
  tick 0
  inst
  targ ov00
*   var1 the middle's x, var2 half the width, var3 the height, var5 the feet
  setv var1 posl
  addv var1 posr
  divv var1 2
  setv var2 posr
  subv var2 posl
  divv var2 2
  setv var3 posb
  subv var3 post
  setv var5 posb
*   west along the shelf to open water, 3-5 px a tick
  loop
    rndv var9 3 5
    subv var1 var9
    doif var1 lt 530 setv var1 530 endi
    setv var4 var1
    subv var4 var2
    setv var6 var5
    subv var6 var3
    mvto var4 var6
    setv vely 0
    wait 1
    inst
    rndv var9 0 7
    doif var9 eq 0
      setv vely 0
      wait 1
      inst
    endi
  untl var1 le 530
*   down through the water to the seabed, 4-7 px a tick
  loop
    rndv var9 4 7
    addv var5 var9
    doif var5 gt 1365 setv var5 1365 endi
    setv var4 var1
    subv var4 var2
    setv var6 var5
    subv var6 var3
    mvto var4 var6
    setv vely 0
    wait 1
    inst
    rndv var9 0 7
    doif var9 eq 0
      setv vely 0
      wait 1
      inst
    endi
  untl var5 ge 1365
*   east along the seabed to the low point, 3-5 px a tick
  loop
    rndv var9 3 5
    addv var1 var9
    doif var1 gt 627 setv var1 627 endi
    setv var4 var1
    subv var4 var2
    setv var6 var5
    subv var6 var3
    mvto var4 var6
    setv vely 0
    wait 1
    inst
  untl var1 ge 627
  setv vely 1
  setv ov93 0
  targ ownr
  kill ownr
endm
* (after a load, no currents are left and no creature counts as carried)
enum 4 0 0 setv ov93 0 setv ov92 0 next
